      "source_excerpt": "protocolSection.descriptionModule, designModule, and outcomesModule: \"A PHASE 3 RANDOMIZED, DOUBLE-BLIND, PLACEBO-CONTROLLED STUDY TO INVESTIGATE THE EFFICACY AND SAFETY OF RITLECITINIB IN PEDIATRIC PARTICIPANTS 6 TO LESS THAN 12 YEARS OF AGE WITH SEVERE ALOPECIA AREATA\" \"During this time, they will have 8 study visits at the study clinic.\" \"The study team will also call participants about 8 times over the phone.\" \"The participants will be assessed for study eligibility at the screening visit after informed consent/assent is obtained (as applicable).\" \"Participants will receive study medication for a duration of 24 weeks.\" \"Participants completing the 24-week treatment period of the study may have the option to enter the long-term extension (LTE) Study B7981028, if the eligibility criteria are met.\" \"Participants who complete the 24-week treatment period of the study but who are ineligible for the LTE study will undergo a 4-week off-treatment follow-up period.\" \"Ritlecitinib higher dose\" \"1 ritlecitinib higher dose capsule once a day (QD) and 1 placebo lower dose capsule once a day (QD) orally for 24 weeks.\" \"Ritlecitinib lower dose\" \"1 ritlecitinib lower dose capsule QD and 1 placebo higher dose capsule QD orally for 24 weeks.\" \"Placebo\" \"1 placebo higher dose capsule QD and 1 placebo lower dose capsule QD orally for 24 weeks.\" \"Week 24\" \"Week 24\" \"Week 2, Week 4, Week 8, Week 12, Week 18, Week 24.\" -- CT.gov describes a screening visit without its duration, a 24-week double-dummy treatment, an optional eligibility-dependent LTE (Study B7981028), and a 4-week off-treatment follow-up for participants ineligible for LTE. Follow-up is conditional and the LTE is a separate study with no stated duration, so total and end-of-study weeks are not fixed. Outcome frames state assessments at Weeks 2, 4, 8, 12, 18 and 24; the brief summary separately reports 8 clinic visits and about 8 phone calls but gives no individual timing for either contact type. The cited CT.gov file contains registry narrative/outcome frames, not a full per-visit schedule table, so full_visit_table_available is false. The registry describes the trial as double-blind and the design masking as quadruple; the treatment periods are also double-dummy based on the arm dosing descriptions. The Week 28 end of the conditional follow-up period is the exact arithmetic 24-week treatment + 4-week follow-up = 28 weeks.",
